{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-38951-r4620072","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Banana Nut Muffins","sourcePageId":38951,"sourceRevision":"4620072","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-23T09:47:04Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Jcb","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Banana%20Nut%20Muffins&oldid=4620072","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:56.684Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baking recipes","Category:CS1 errors: invisible characters","Category:CS1 maint: multiple names: authors list","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for muffins","Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using banana","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using molasses","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes using whole-wheat flour","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Vegetarian recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"e4edb34b39caf3e57b58334626d03e8732b19887fed06cfe5cdd23717b57a1b5","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Muffin recipes|yield=20 ea. 2-inch muffins|time=Prep: ~15 minutes<br/>Baking: 20-25 minutes|difficulty=2\n| Image = [[Image:Banana-Nut-Muffins-2005-Aug-24.jpg|300px|Two muffins prepared from this recipe.]]\n}}{{recipe}}\n\nA recipe for '''banana nut muffins''', based on one from the Joy of Cooking<ref>{{cite book|title=Joy of Cooking|author=Rombauer, Irma S. and Rombauer Becker, Marion|publisher=The Bobbs-Merrill Company|year=1975|id={{#isbn:0026045702}}}}</ref>, but slightly modified.\n\n==Ingredients==\n*2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]] [[cookbook:honey|honey]], [[cookbook:molasses|molasses]], or [[cookbook:sugar|sugar]]\n*1 cup [[cookbook:milk|milk]] (or [[Cookbook:Soy Milk|soy milk]])\n*¼ cup [[cookbook:vegetable oil|vegetable oil]]\n*2–3 [[Cookbook:Banana|bananas]], [[Cookbook:Mashing|mashed]]\n*⅔ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (160 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) [[Cookbook:Flour|white flour]]\n*1⅓ cups (320 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[cookbook:Whole Wheat|whole wheat flour]]\n*½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*2 tsp [[cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n*½ cups (120 ml) chopped [[Cookbook:Nuts and seeds|nuts]] (such as [[cookbook:walnut|walnut]]s)\n*[[cookbook:sugar|Sugar]] to taste, if necessary\n\n==Procedure==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven Temperatures|400°F (200°C)]].\n# Grease a [[Cookbook:Muffin Pan|muffin tin]].\n# [[Cookbook:Creaming|Cream]] together eggs, honey, milk, vegetable oil, and bananas. \n# Combine dry ingredients, then mix gently with wet ingredients. Lumpy batter is to be expected.\n# [[cookbook:Baking|Bake]] for 20–25 minutes.\n# Cool.\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n[[Category:Recipes using banana]]\n[[Category:Recipes for muffins]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whole-wheat flour]